  "market_context": "Analyst reviews multiple Bitcoin bull cycles on the daily chart, highlighting historical retracements during strong uptrends. Emphasizes this is a long-term position strategy, not intraday trading, aimed at buying dips for faster value accumulation.",
  "key_observation": "Every major bull run on BTC/USDT daily chart retraced to either the 0.5 or 0.618 Fibonacci level before resuming upward momentum; only one setup resulted in a stop-out among all observed rallies.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: The analyst switched from 1-hour to daily timeframe to examine long-term structure of Bitcoin bull runs.",
    "Step 2: Identified four major upward impulses on the daily chart and drew Fibonacci retracements from each swing low to swing high.",
    "Step 3: Observed that three of the four retracements ended precisely at the 0.5 level, one at 0.618, and one resulted in a stop-out.",
    "Step 4: Concluded that Fibonacci retracement levels (especially 0.5–0.618) reliably mark dip-buying zones for long-term crypto positions."
  ],
  "outcome": "One stop-out among all setups; otherwise successful long-term buy-the-dip entries.",
  "lessons": "Fibonacci retracements on daily charts provide high-probability long-term entry zones for crypto assets; consistent application yields strong risk-adjusted returns despite occasional stop-outs.",
